0 carts (Brickwright Robot Lab validation machine, round 2)
0 Name: carts.ldr
0 Author: Brickwright
0 !LDRAW_ORG Unofficial_Model
0 // Two free carts ahead of the shipped SPIKE driving base (static/sim-lab/models/driving-base.ldr, copied unchanged
0 // below; forward is LDraw +z). Each cart: a Technic beam 15 on its edge along z (holes along x) at axle height,
0 // its ends (+-149 LDU) the bumpers; a 6L rear axle at -60 with SPIKE wheels 39367p01 (radius 70 LDU) at x = +-30
0 // and an 8L front axle at +60 with wheels at x = +-70 (front and rear wheels side by side, so the wheelbase is
0 // shorter than a tyre diameter and the tyres stay inside the bumpers: the carts meet beam end to beam end).
0 // Cart 1 (centre z = 250): its rear tyres 10 LDU (4 mm) ahead of the hub's front face (z = 110); the robot pushes
0 // it by them. Cart 2 (centre z = 598): its rear bumper 50 LDU (20 mm) ahead of cart 1's front bumper. The carts
0 // are loose by design. Mass per cart: beam 4.8 g + axles 0.8 + 1.0 g + wheels 4 x 12 g.
